# Bidding round

A bidding round lets members pledge a price per <%= Basket.model_name.human.downcase %> for their <%= BasketSize.model_name.human.downcase %>, based on what they can afford while helping cover the organization's needs.

Pledged amounts are constrained by configurable min/max bounds.

## Requirements {#requirements}

- Memberships for the new season must be created and the first delivery must be in the future.
- Only one bidding round can be open at a time.

> Members flagged as "<%= Member.human_attribute_name(:salary_basket) %>" are automatically excluded from bidding rounds, since their membership price is zeroed out.

Before opening a bidding round, check the following in the [settings](/settings#bidding_round):

- Minimum <%= BasketSize.model_name.human.downcase %> price (0-100%) — defines the minimum allowed percentage.
- Maximum <%= BasketSize.model_name.human.downcase %> price (0-X%) — defines the maximum allowed percentage.
- Send a reminder after (in days).

These settings ensure a consistent frame for member pledges and enable automated reminders during the opening period.

> The default pledge is the previous round's pledge if there is one, otherwise the [<%= BasketSize.model_name.human.downcase %> price](/basket_sizes). Min and max use that same size price. A custom amount already on the membership is ignored until you click "Complete" and the pledges are written.

## Flow {#flow}

1. Create memberships for the new season (see [renewal](/handbook/membership_renewal)).
2. Create and open a new bidding round.
3. Let members pledge amounts for their <%= BasketSize.model_name.human(count: 2).downcase %> (the duration of the opening window is up to you).
4. Review the results of the bidding round and decide:
   - Are the needs covered? Finish the bidding round to update the price per <%= Basket.model_name.human.downcase %> for all memberships that received a pledge.
   - Needs not covered? Close (failure) the bidding round and create a new one.

## Opening {#opening}

When the bidding round is opened, an automatic email is sent to members. From their accounts, they can access a form to pledge the price for their <%= BasketSize.model_name.human.downcase %>.

### Reminder

A reminder can be sent automatically while the bidding round is open. The delay counts from when the round was **created**, not from when it was opened. A draft that sat for those days can remind as soon as you open it.

## Finish (success) {#finish}

When the bidding round is finished (success), the price per <%= Basket.model_name.human.downcase %> is updated for all memberships that received a pledge. Memberships without a pledge are not modified.

An automatic email (optional) can be sent to every eligible member, pledge or not.

## Close (failure) {#close}

When the bidding round is closed (failure), no membership is modified. You can then open a new bidding round to try to converge on a price acceptable to all members.

An automatic email (optional) can be sent to every eligible member, pledge or not.
